# .gitignore — toolkit/
#
# Template-owned; copier update keeps it current. Project-wide rules belong in the root .gitignore.
# No inline comments in this file: Git reads a # after a pattern as part of the pattern.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written by python3 when media.py imports its helper modules: machine-specific and regenerable.
# The rule sits here rather than in the root .gitignore because the root file belongs to
# whichever template wrote it first, and the toolkit is media's own.
/__pycache__/
